1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,200
Hey, welcome back! In this video I'll show you
how to set up Acme in under five minutes.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,800
There are three steps: connect your account,
build a form, and turn on alerts.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,400
Step one, connect your account.
Open the Acme dashboard and click Settings.

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,900
Now paste your API key into this field.
Don't share it with anyone.

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,800
Then press Command K to open quick search.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,200
Type "integrations" and select the first result.

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,600
Hit Connect, and wait for it to sync.
This takes a minute.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,300
Okay, it's done. Notice the green status badge
in the top right corner.

9
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,600
Moving on. Step two, build your first form.

10
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:34,200
Click the plus button, then choose Form from the menu.

11
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,800
Add an email field and a phone number field,
then press Enter to save.

12
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:41,500
Here's the thing: shorter forms convert better.
Always ask for less!

13
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,200
Before, our test form had nine fields.
After we cut it to three, sign-ups went up 42%.

14
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,900
That's an extra $1,200 a month from the same traffic.

15
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,400
Now let's do step three, turn on alerts.

16
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,100
Open the Alerts tab and toggle on New Submission.

17
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,700
Every time someone fills out the form,
you'll get a notification on your phone.

18
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,200
You can even send them a text message reply automatically.

19
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,800
So to recap: connect your account, build a short form,
and turn on alerts.

20
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,400
The template I used is linked in the description below.

21
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:13,600
Thanks for watching, and I'll see you in the next video!
